<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  File Provider extension entitlements for RELEASE builds (release automation).

  Identical to FileProviderExtension.entitlements except that
  com.apple.developer.fileprovider.testing-mode is deliberately ABSENT.

  Two reasons, and the first is fatal rather than cosmetic:

  1. testing-mode is a restricted entitlement. Apple grants it only through a
     *development* provisioning profile, so a Developer ID profile — the kind a
     notarized, publicly distributed build must use — does not include it, and
     codesign fails with "provisioning profile doesn't include the
     com.apple.developer.fileprovider.testing-mode entitlement".
  2. It should not ship anyway. It exists so the acceptance suite can drive
     NSFileProviderDomain.testingModes and waitForStabilization deterministically
     (progress.md AC-3, Task 6.1); that is a developer capability, not a user one.

  Everything else must stay identical to the Debug file: the app group and keychain
  group are what let the containing app's sign-in hand credentials to the extension
  (Tasks 2.5, 5.1), and network.client is what makes every WebDAV/Graph request
  possible at all. Keep the two files in step when either changes.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)group.com.owncloud.macos.fileprovider</string>
    </array>
    <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.owncloud.macos.fileprovider.shared</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
